  "task": {
    "name": "Sprint live status shows complexity as a number for stories in DEV, a band word for stories in other phases",
    "slug": "issue-1917",
    "story_path": null,
    "story_text": "## Observed behavior\n\nIn the live sprint status dashboard, the COMPLEXITY column shows a raw numeric score for some story rows and a band word for others, within the same table render of the same run.\n\n## Expected behavior\n\nWhenever a story has a computed numeric complexity score, every phase's live-state update should carry that score, so the display's preference for the numeric form holds uniformly for a story in any phase \u2014 not only for stories that have passed through DEV. Applying this must not clear a score that has already been established for a story.\n\n## Diagnosis\n\n- **Observed symptom:** the live sprint-status COMPLEXITY column renders a bare integer for some rows and a band-label word for others, in the same table, at the same moment.\n- **Evidence:** run `78f9b1883f00`. The per-story audits for #1899, #1910 and #1911 each record a numeric complexity score (5, 6, 6), yet #1911 rendered `medium` while #1899 and #1910 rendered their numbers. #1911 was in PLAN_REVIEW and had never entered DEV; #1910 was in REVIEW, reachable only by way of DEV.\n- **Ruled out:** the adaptive-routing changes in the same release window \u2014 they alter routing decisions, not status-display plumbing, and touch none of the modules involved. Also ruled out: the display renderer, which correctly prefers a numeric score whenever one is present \u2014 #1911 proves a score existed in coordinator state and still did not reach the renderer.\n- **Confirmed cause:** the coordinator builds its live-state update payload separately in each phase module, and only the DEV-phase payloads include the numeric score alongside the band label; every other phase's payload carries the band alone. Because the sprint state writer ignores keys absent from an update, a score written during DEV persists for the remainder of the run, while a story that has not reached DEV has no score in live state at all \u2014 so a single render mixes both forms. This is the uncompleted remainder of the earlier fix for #1364, which added the score to the DEV payloads and the display path but left the sibling phase modules untouched.\n- **Affected code path:** the per-phase live-state update payload construction across the coordinator's phase modules (preflight, plan, review, validate), the reviewer progress channel used by the plan-review and review pools, which carries no score field at all, and the sprint state writer's per-field update handling.\n- **Fix-success criterion:** in a live sprint, a story's COMPLEXITY cell shows its numeric score as soon as one has been computed for it, in any phase, including stories that terminate without ever entering DEV; and no update path clears a score that was already set.\n\n## Hazard\n\nAt least one preflight payload is constructed before the score has been computed, and the state writer treats an explicit null as an instruction to clear. A uniform \"carry the key everywhere\" change would therefore wipe an established score on the mid-sprint preflight re-run path. The fix has to establish when the score is known, not merely where the key is absent.\n",
    "github_issue": 1917,
    "fix_ready": true,
    "readiness_warnings": []
  },
